Unless otherwise prohibited by State or Federal law, the Planning Commission may grant a variance from the rules and regulations governing Class 2, 3, and 4 special use permits if the Planning Commission makes a finding that compliance with any provision would:
(1) Result in an arbitrary and unreasonable taking of property;
(2) Result, in effect, in the closing and elimination of any lawful business, occupation or activity without sufficient corresponding benefit or advantage to the public;
(3) Cause an unnecessary hardship;
(4) Not substantially further the purposes of this chapter because of extraordinary and exceptional conditions pertaining to the particular piece of property in question because of its size, shape or topography.
(Code 2005, § 34-390; Ord. of 7-20-1994, § 7.05)

